      "writtenOn": "2026-11-14T01:12:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two selection edge cases in `resolveRangeTarget` can anchor drafts to the wrong line: (1) because `endCell` itself carries `data-line`, `endEl.closest(\u0027[data-line]\u0027)` matches `endCell` whenever a drag ends on a `.line-placeholder` or other child without `data-line`, making `startEl.closest(\u0027[data-line]\u0027)` unreachable and jumping back to the block\u0027s `startLine`; and (2) triple-clicking line `N` sets `range.endContainer` on line `N + 1` with `endOffset \u003d\u003d\u003d 0`, anchoring the comment to line `N + 1`. Consider excluding `endCell` when checking inner `[data-line]` ancestors before falling back to `startEl`, and adjusting when `range.endOffset \u003d\u003d\u003d 0` and `startContainer !\u003d\u003d endContainer`.",
