      "message": "Treating every `\u003cident\u003e!\"...\"` as an interpolated string here and in `advanceLeanLexState` (line 2094) flips quote parity when a `!`-suffixed macro or function such as `panic!` takes an ordinary string containing `{`. For example, `def msg :\u003d panic!\"{\"\\ntheorem bad : False :\u003d by sorry\\ndef endMsg :\u003d \"}\"` enters `interpBraceDepths` at `{` and opens `inString \u003d true` on the closing `\"`, blanking out `sorry` and producing a false `0 sorry` verified badge. Should this match only Lean\u0027s string interpolators (`s!`, `m!`, `f!`), consistent with `tokenizeLeanLine` at line 2933?",
