      "message": "`parseLeanBlocks` absorbs any subsequent line with `curIndent \u003e declIndent` (including across blank lines at line 2599) into the current declaration, while `analyzeDeclarationHygiene` (lines 1579–1581) checks only the outer header\u0027s `kind` and `modifiers` for `axiom`, `partial`, and `unsafe`. Valid Lean 4 such as `theorem clean : 1 + 1 \u003d 2 :\u003d rfl\\n\\n  axiom bad : False` (or same-line `theorem clean : True :\u003d (trivial) axiom bad : False`) merges `bad` into `clean`\u0027s collapsible proof body and renders a green `0 sorry` verified badge. Consider breaking out of the continuation loop when a new declaration/directive starts with balanced delimiters, and checking `ids.has(\u0027axiom\u0027 | \u0027partial\u0027 | \u0027unsafe\u0027)` in `analyzeDeclarationHygiene`.",
