      "message": "`blockStartLine` uses nullish coalescing instead of `Math.min(...)` across non-empty pending items, so when a standalone modifier precedes `@[...]` (e.g. adding `unsafe` on line 1 above `@[simp]\\ndef foo : Nat :\u003d 1`), `blockStartLine` evaluates to `2` and `lines.slice(blockStartLine - 1, blockEndLine)` omits line 1 from `block.raw`—causing `alignLeanBlocks` to mark the block `unchanged` and breaking line-1 thread attachment. Also note that `--` comments at line 2385 call `flushPendingAsStandalone()`, detaching preceding modifiers or docstrings from the declaration. Consider taking `Math.min(...)` across present pending start lines and preserving pending docs/attributes/modifiers across intervening `--` comments.",
