      "message": "`renderLeanLineWithInlineDiff` assumes `common` + `editType` segments sum to `fullLine.length`, but `coalesceInlineDiffSegments` drops `common` whitespace from the opposite side when merging two pure `added` or pure `deleted` runs (for example, diffing `def f ( ) : 𝔸 :\u003d oldVal` vs `def f (a b) : 𝔸 :\u003d newVal`). Each dropped space shifts `pos` left for the rest of the line, misaligning `\u003cdel\u003e`/`\u003cins\u003e` highlights and potentially slicing astral Unicode math symbols (`𝔸`) mid-surrogate-pair at line 3196. Consider building the per-side edit mask directly from `rawDiff` (and coalescing whitespace runs on that per-side mask) so `pos` stays 1:1 with `fullLine`.",
