      "message": "`alignLeanCodeLines` (along with `alignStructureFields` at line 3319 and `blockPairScore` at line 3623) scores similarity via `computeNormalizedEditDistance`, whose `/\\w/` token filter drops non-ASCII Lean identifiers (`α`, `β`, `γ`) and math operators (`∀`, `≤`, `→`, `⟨`, `⟩`). As a result, `| ⟨α, β, γ⟩ \u003d\u003e ⟨α, β, γ⟩` vs `| ⟨α, β, γ⟩ \u003d\u003e ⟨α, β, γ + 1⟩` gets distance `1.0` and fails to pair, while unrelated lines `have : α \u003d β` and `have : ∀ γ δ, γ ⊆ δ` both filter to `[\u0027have\u0027]` with distance `0.0`. Should Lean alignment use a Unicode-aware content token check (e.g. `/[\\p{L}\\p{N}_]/u` plus math operators)?",
